course: dictionary
lesson: 201
title: Words that name a place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where something comes from. Alaskan is one of them: it tells you something is from Alaska, or about Alaska. Alaska is the largest state in the USA, in the far north-west of North America.
explain: Look at the clues in «a wood frog freezes solid in the Alaskan winter». The word winter tells you the place is cold, and Alaskan tells you which winter it is: the winter in Alaska. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Alaskan can also be a noun. An Alaskan is a person who lives in or comes from Alaska, and the plural is Alaskans. Watch the word around it to tell which kind it is: if it describes a thing, it is an adjective; if it names a person, it is a noun.
fact: Alaskan is an adjective when it describes something, like Alaskan bears or Alaskan salmon.
fact: An Alaskan is a noun: a person who lives in or comes from Alaska. The plural is Alaskans.
fact: Alaska is the largest state in the USA, in the far north-west of North America.
fact: «Alaskan wilderness» means the wild nature of Alaska.
fact: «Alaskan Malamute» is a breed of dog named after Alaska.
exercise: «a wood frog freezes solid in the Alaskan winter» What does Alaskan describe here? | *The winter in Alaska | The spring weather | A kind of frog food | A frog from Cameroon
exercise: Where is Alaska? | In the south of Africa | On an island in Australia | *In the far north-west of North America | In the middle of Europe
exercise: What is a person who lives in Alaska called? | A glacier | A Malamute | A Cameroonian | *An Alaskan
test: «The Alaskan Malamute pulled the sledge through the snow.» What kind of word is Alaskan here? | An adverb, describing how the dog moved | A noun, meaning a person | *An adjective, describing the dog | A verb, meaning to pull
test: Maya says her cousin is an Alaskan. What does she mean? | Her cousin is a large glacier | Her cousin is a kind of bear | Her cousin has a cold on a spring day | *Her cousin lives in or comes from Alaska
exam: Which phrase means the same as «Alaskan wilderness»? | The busy streets of a city in Alaska | The wild nature of Cameroon | *The wild nature of Alaska | A wooden house by the sea
